      "writtenOn": "2023-05-23T16:48:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "return -ENOMEM\n\nHowever, you don\u0027t need this buffer. You are reading record by record into nextMsgLine, then aggregating them into kernelBuffer and then copying into userspace buffer using copy_to_user(). You can copy from nextMsgLine directly into userspace buffer instead:\n```\n  size_t bytes_copied \u003d 0;\n  ...\n  temp_size \u003d snprintf(nextMsgLine, ...);\n  if (temp_size + bytes_copied \u003e\u003d count)\n    break;\n  copy_to_user(buf + bytes_copied, nextMsgLine, temp_size);\n  bytes_copied +\u003d temp_size;\n  ... \n```",
