      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can have many pollers which will be passing different `filp`. therefore `last_oom_kill_data_poll` can\u0027t be global. If has to be tied to the `filep`.\n\nLucky for you, struct file has a member called `private_data` where you can stash your `last_oom_kill_data_poll`. You will have to define `proc_open` and `proc_release` callbacks for `oom_kills_list_proc_ops` and inside `proc_open` handler you should allocate `filep-\u003eprivate_data` and inside `proc_release` handler you should free it.",
